1.141.m:
Vyāsa said:
All those young boys of the Bhojakas were questioned by you;
what was then told by them? Tell me that in full.

1.148.m:
Vāsudeva said:
The lotus indeed has six petals by virtue of the six seasons, and rests on the imperishable [axle];
it is presided over by the Spirit, and the Sun with his limbs is situated there.
